1_Ship: Brig (Floor 1)_You wake up on a lumpy bottom bunk inside a cramped room, without a moment’s rest. The air is thick with the stench of sweat, the only sound being the steady beat of waves against the ship. You sit in a small, cramped cell that is unguarded but locked, preventing you from leaving. The cell has two bunks, the other being occupied by another nameless prisoner. The prisoner sits opposite you, and looks at you with anticipation, as though he has something to tell you. After the player recruits the Prisoner: You look behind you at your cramped, smelly prison cell. With the cell door unlocked, the ladder leading up to the top deck appears to be your only way out._2,0,0,0
2_Ship: Top Deck(Floor 2)_You emerge from your cell to be greeted with your first view of the island, the Summit towering over you in the distance. The fresh breeze hits your face on the upper deck. Bare metal railings surround the edges of the ship. Beyond them are dark blue waves with no land in sight._3,0,1,0
3_Southern Shores_As you run down the gangplank, hoping not to draw any attention, your feet finally meet the damp sand. The gentle rise of incoming waves laps at your ankles. Guards can be heard just behind you, making small talk somewhere else in the ship. Further down the coast to the right, a small marine village sits nestled against the shore, its distant details blurred by the sea haze. The only way forward seems to be through the large cave to the North._4,0,0,0
4_Mines: Entrance_You step out into a cavernous pit of black rock, where the air burns your lungs with crystal dust. Tiny mana crystals embedded in the walls cast a dim glow over exhausted prisoners swinging pickaxes against unyielding stone. A sharp, echoing crack of a heavy whip rings out, followed by the booming voice of the taskmaster berating an elderly prisoner for not making progress fast enough. The captain continues leading the line of new prisoners deeper into the cave without batting an eye._5,0,3,0
5_Mines: Quarry_In front of you lies a vast pit with a vast spiral staircase carved into the stones leading down to the bottom of the quarry. There are numerous floors to the mines visible within the pit, with various laborers and minecart tracks moving throughout. On the other side of the pit, blocking the exit to the North, stands what appears to be the Taskmaster of the mines, wearing soot-covered armor and brandishing a spiked mace in one hand, and a long rusted chain in the other._6,0,0,0
6_Palm Forest_The sweltering heat of the mines dissipates as you step out of the darkness into the Sun’s warm embrace. As your eyes adjust you take note of the many palm trees towering above you, with coconuts littered and strewn about the sand. You catch a vague scent of the ocean and can hear waves gently breaking in the distance, along with the occasional cry from the seagulls._7,8,0,0
7_Rugged Path_You walk through patches of dull green grass and step out onto a rugged path. Before taking a step, you look down carefully to make sure you won’t lose your footing on the uneven terrain. As you walk, you can feel the sharp edges of each stone pressing firmly against the soles of your shoes. The way forward is slow and requires some focus to get through the landscape._14,11,0,0
8_Marine Town Center_You step onto the wooden planks of a coastal harbor village built entirely on elevated platforms above the turquoise sea. Colorful awnings stretch over bustling market stalls trading fish, weapons, and potions. The air carries the pleasant aroma of roasting meat and sea salt under a cloudy sky._10,9,0,6
9_Shipyard_Before the player has recruited the Mariner: The stall is dark inside. Long tables are stacked with crates of fish and tangled fishnets. The smell of salt is stronger in here. A Mariner sits alone at a stall, sharpening an axe. After the player has recruited the Mariner: The stall is dark inside. Long tables are stacked with crates of fish and tangled fishnets. The smell of salt is stronger in here._0,0,0,8
10_Commercial District_You go to the back of the longest line in the village. When it’s your turn, a man with an eye patch looks up from behind a table stacked with crates. “Take a look.” He gestures at the crates. “Whatever you want, if it’s here, hand me something of equal worth and it’s yours.”_0,0,8,0
11_Archives (Floor 1)_You push open a pair of towering dark brown doors into a vast hall lined with endless shelves of leather-bound books reaching into the ceiling far above. The scent of old parchment and leather fills the air. Small candles and pale rays of moonlight illuminate the dark room, wrapped in the heavy silence. On the left wall by the entrance is a massive mural of a man wearing a regal set of armor with gold trim and a luxurious red cape, planting a blood-red banner onto the sand of what you assume is this island, with a symbol that depicts a hollow sun in its center, surrounded by knights looking up at him as a ray of light emanates from his body and into the dark. You turn to see a woman with tired eyes behind big spectacles, wearing a weary, disgruntled expression. She slides one of the books from her arms back onto a shelf. “No, no.” she mutters to herself. “This can’t be right, I can’t make any sense of this at all…”_12,17,0,7
12_Archives (Floor 2)_This floor looks just like the one below it, but the rows of books on surface-level topics like history, calligraphy, and scribing are replaced with more specialized knowledge like weapons, tactics, and theory. On the right, by the door, is another large mural. It shows Sol Invictus forming an alliance with the people of the Island. Sol is standing in the center of the Marine Town, in front of the fountain. His men are lined up behind him in a troop formation, one man in front holding the same banner shown in the mural downstairs. In front of Sol stands a lone figure, someone who appears to be a laborer, wearing dirty, weathered rags. The man extends both arms to offer a sword to Sol, while the rest of the people of the Island are all lined up behind him, kneeling to their new Lord. Beyond the mural, on the far right of the room, stairs lead up to a door with a sign reading: "The Archmage’s Chambers. No Entry."_13,0,11,0
13_Archives: Archmage's Quarters (Floor 3)_The door creaks. You slip inside and hold your breath. A third mural hangs high on the wall, this one showing Sol Invictus' victory over the Great Serpent. It depicts Sol in his regal armor, standing atop the summit with the sun rising over the hills behind him. At his feet, a serpent lies impaled on the spear he’s holding. Below the mural, an empty semicircular desk sits in the center of the room with magic artifacts arranged in neat rows upon it. Two identical wizard robes are laid out across the table. Beyond the desk, round shelves hold books older than anything on the lower floors. You step cautiously to the nearest shelf, your companions close behind. Footsteps echo from a distant shelf. You peek around the edge and catch the back of a hooded figure._0,0,12,0
14_Ancestral Woods: Grove_You arrive at the deepest part of the woods, a dark grove surrounded by tall, gnarled trees stuck closely together. Your shoes sink into the dark, soggy soil among patches of dead grass. The eerie sounds of monsters are very loud despite it being so dark._0,15,7,0
15_Ancestral Woods: Thicket_You go out into the woods, into a thick cloak of fog obscures the sparse, twisted trees. Your shoes are muddied by the dark soggy soil, the only plants in sight being dark soggy soil. Thorny branches catch on your clothes. Faint, eerie sounds of monsters echo in all directions, and none of you have any idea of where to go. After several minutes of walking in circles, bumping into fallen logs, and sharing puzzled, anxious glances, you’re forced to see the truth: you’re lost._0,16,0,14
16_Ancestral Woods: Clearing_You step out from the dark forest into an open clearing where a thin layer of fog creeps over dead grass and dark, soggy soil. Despite the light, the sounds of monsters remind you that you probably shouldn't stay here too long._0,0,18,15
17_Smithy_As you walk through the woods, you catch a glimpse of a smoke rising in the distance. You follow it to a low brick building beside a river, a worn wooden sign over the door. It might be worth looking inside. A wave of hot air hits your face as you step in. A few feet away, bright orange flames blaze in the forge. Nearby, the Blacksmith hammers a piece of glowing iron, sweat beading on his brow with every blow._18,19,0,11
18_Sanguine River_You step out toward the edge of the Sanguine River. The dark water flows steadily past the low brick building of the smithy and winds its way back into the dense forest. A faint, fresh scent hangs heavy on the damp breeze rising off the current. The path alongside the water is slick and slightly muddy, but it offers a clear route to explore further._16,0,17,0
19_Mountain Village_The bell jingles overhead as you push through the door. Behind a counter is a middle aged man with a long brown beard. He gives you a calculated smile and gestures at the shelves behind him. “I’m passing through. Picked up a lot of goods on the road. What are you looking for? I’ll give anything for the right price.”_24,27,20,17
20_Depths: Entrance (Floor 1)_Tall black rock with jagged edges loom over you. Rivers of fire pour down the walls onto a bed of lava below. Imprinted on the upper rock, looming over the entire chamber, is a painting of a warrior-king standing atop the summit with a sword raised to the sky in one hand and fire in the other, the Brand of the Gods on his chest. In the center of the cave is a massive ring of cliff opens into darkness. Distant muffled screams rise from below. A corpse drags itself from behind a rock._19,0,21,0
21_Depths (Floor 2)_As you fall further down, the screams grow louder, piercing the thick, choking mist. The condemned are tortured endlessly, enclosed in a void without end. Another painting is imprinted on the rock: a man in primitive clothes standing over a raging fire in the center of a dark forest, a solemn look on his face as if he had gained deep insight from the flames. On the other side, a group of people in rags cower from the fire. Despite their fear, the huddled masses seem inexplicably drawn toward it.A wailing sound drifts from the mist nearby._20,0,22,0
22_Depths (Floor 3)_Your ears ring from the nonstop screams. Sure enough, there is another painting, older than the ones before, faintly illuminated by the lava. A single figure in the dark, wearing white robes and a golden wreath, reaches down toward a small flame, fingers almost touching it as the rest of her body angles upward, retreating into the clouds. The other two figures are already in the clouds, looking back towards her, waiting._21,0,23,0
23_Depths: Tartarus (Floor 4)_Like all the other floors, the ground opens into a cliff in the center, but instead of a lower floor, there is a wall of flame, and beneath it, darkness. Nothing can be heard from below, only the muffled screams from the upper floors. You look back up. The floor is almost empty, except for a prisoner chained to the wall, several scars across his chest and wounds all over his face, wearing the Brand of the gods. A golden spear lies on the ground at his feet. His chains are long enough to reach it, but not long enough to leave the room. Imprinted on the rock behind him is one last painting: the same three figures from above, arms outstretched toward the Leviathan. Three golden spears pierce its body._22,0,0,0
24_Northern Shores_You take one last breath, grip your companions’ hands, and walk toward the whirlpool. It catches you. You close your eyes as the water churns and the world goes dark. A second later, you feel rough, jagged ground beneath your feet. You open your eyes._25,0,19,0
25_Oracle Island: Shores_As you step off the boat, crushed sand crunches under your feet. Imposing stone columns and monuments guard the entrance to the sacred stone temple, flanked by stone pavilions. Behind them, a dense green forest can be seen, but no path leads in. Far out along the coast, a low shape sits in the water. It doesn’t look like rock._26,0,24,0
