27_Meadow_As the tree line around the mountain thins out, a meadow comes into view. Daisies and dandelions sway in the wind. At the edge of the grass, a small clearing holds a fire pit still smoldering. A piece of meat sits on a log, still warm. In the distance is a broken altar, not too far from the Smoldering Ruins. This looks like a perfect place to rest before taking on the Final Battle._0,28,0,19
28_Smoldering Ruins: Entrance (Room 1)_At the end of the meadow, a damaged stone floor leads up to a temple. Crumbling doric columns frame the open ceiling, intricate carvings fading into the limestone walls. At the entrance, two Centurions, Sol Invictus’ elite knights, guard the opening._29,0,0,0
29_Smoldering Ruins: Citadel (Room 2)_You run past the guards into a large limestone interior space with broken statues of the Gods and burned remnants of paintings spread throughout the crumbling walls. At the back is a pair of grand double doors with two Praetorians guarding them. Your companions stand on either side of you at the ready._30,0,0,0
30_Smoldering Ruins: Throne Room (Room 3)_The grand doors open to reveal a large ashen crater where the Throne Room once was. At the far end, buried in debris, is a throne of stone. It’s cracked down the middle, parts of the arms chipped away. Two Praetorians, the best of the elite, stand on either side of it. Behind the throne, five shallow graves can be seen, each with a sword half-buried in the ground, the blade full of rust. A shield lies on top of the burial mound with faded color. On the throne sits a burned husk of a man, wearing old rusted armor too large for the withering figure, tarnished golden accents and bits of burned red cloth peeking through the cracks in the armor. His head is tilted forward, his eyes fixed on the center of the crater, where a golden sconce stands out from the ash. The Flame of the Gods is only cinders now, with bits of white smoke barely visible around the edges of the sconce._0,0,0,0